Railcraft mainline development for 1.12 is in hiatus, and there are bugs to be fixed.

So here it is.

As of now, it:

- Fixes custom rolling machine recipes with certain size being incorrectly displayed in JEI.
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2120)
- Aggressively fixes FPS drop when some Railcraft machines are running, e.g. boiler.
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2121)
- Allows worldspike to stack fuels to item's own maximum stack size (works in GUI and automation)
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2082)
- Fixes some outfitted track GUIs showing raw translation key as title
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2097)
- Fixes crash upon opening GUI of RF Loader / Unloader, making them usable
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2098)
- Fixes "Carts" label flying out of window in Activator Track GUI
- Fixes crashes when breaking bottom layer of a completed water tank
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2101 - courtesy of ACGaming)
- Fixes Steam Turbine not forming when using IC2Classic
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2040 - courtesy of Speiger)
- Fixes tooltips are not shown in Steel Anvil GUI
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2093 - courtesy of ACGaming)
- Provides alternative recipes for electrodes, allowing inputs to be in any column
  (3TUSK/RailwayDeoptWorker#1)
- Fixes loots in minecarts being duplicated in mineshaft generation
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#1810 - courtesy of jchung01)
- Automatically revives MystCraft dimensions that has Worldspike (aka World Anchor) in it after server restart
  (3TUSK/RailwayDeoptWorker#6)
- Fixes Hopper Cart duplicating items
  (3TUSK/RailwayDeoptWorker#9)
- Provides config options to solve the ExU2 missing fluid texture issue
  (3TUSK/RailwayDeoptWorker#10, Kanzaji/XU2-Patcher#1)
- Fixes discrepency in Cargo Cart dismantling; now it gives back Redstone Comparator, which is used in crafting.
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2066)
- Fixes incompatiblity with optimization mods that changes BlockPos#hashCode behavior, making powered machine usable again 
  (Railcraft/Railcraft#2123, 3TUSK/RailwayDeoptWorker#11)
- Fixes water input slots in Steam Locomotive GUI, making them usable again
  (3TUSK/RailwayDeoptWorker#13)

This mod works in Minecraft 1.12.2 ONLY.

This mod works with either the original Railcraft, or ACGaming's fork.

This mod, along with its source, is released in public domain.
You can certainly use it in modpacks.

------

FAQ

Q: Do you accept new features, like a new cart or a new locomotive?
A: Unfortunately no. 
   This mod intends to fix issues left in Railcraft; it does not want new features (unless for fixing things). 
   New contents should be in a separate addon mod, in my opinion.

Q: What does that "betaMessage" mean in config file?
A: There are three (3) possible options for that config option:

  1. lite
     This is the default behavior. 
     Replace the beta warning with our warning, saying all Railcraft issues should be reported to 
     Railway Depot Worker (here) first, if the Railway Depot Worker mod is installed.
     Also it makes the beta warning translatable.
     Also it makes beta warning appear only once for every player.
  2. original
     Do not touch the beta message. This is the original Railcraft behavior.
  3. off
     Turns off everything. 
     Useful if you are making a modpack; in this case, you want all issues in your modpack to go to modpack author (i.e. you) first.

Q: Do you have a changelog?
A: Unfortunately, no. 
   The idea is that you always want the latest version, so that you can have all the fixes and the new fixes.
   I will try find some time to (retroactively) create a proper one, though. 

